.TH RNDIS-TETHER 1 "2026-11-06" "TetherMac" "General Commands Manual"
.SH NAME
rndis-tether \- USB tethering from Android phones on macOS
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B rndis-tether
[\fB\-rwa4v\fR]
[\fB\-U\fR \fIuser\fR]
[\fB\-S\fR \fIserial\fR]
[\fB\-W\fR \fIuser\fR]
[\fB\-d\fR \fIvid\fR:\fIpid\fR]
.br
.B rndis-tether
\fB\-\-version\fR | \fB\-V\fR
.br
.B rndis-tether
\fB\-\-diagnose\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B rndis-tether
gives the Mac internet access through an Android phone's USB tethering, without any kernel extension.
It speaks RNDIS to the phone through libusb, handles DHCP, ARP and IPv6 neighbor discovery itself,
and exposes the link as a
.BR utun (4)
interface.
.PP
It must run as root.
It is normally installed as a LaunchDaemon by
.B tethermac-install
(or
.BR install.sh ),
with the options
.BR "\-r \-w \-a" .
.PP
The program is split in two processes.
A small
.I supervisor
runs as root: it creates the interface, applies network configuration after validating every value,
and cleans up.
A
.I worker
runs as an unprivileged user and does all the parsing of data coming from the phone and the network.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-r
Send all traffic through the phone (split routes 0.0.0.0/1 and 128.0.0.0/1, and ::/1 and 8000::/1 for IPv6)
and apply the phone's DNS server.
Both are removed when the session ends.
.TP
.B \-w
Wait for a phone and reconnect after it is unplugged.
.TP
.B \-a
Enable USB tethering on the phone with
.BR adb (1)
when no RNDIS device is found. USB debugging must be enabled and authorised.
.TP
.B \-4
IPv4 only: do not relay IPv6.
.TP
.B \-L
With
.BR \-r ,
let IPv6 leave through the Mac's other networks when the tether has no IPv6.
By default IPv6 towards the Internet is then blocked with two reject routes, so that applications fall back to IPv4 through the phone.
.TP
.B \-O
Accept a phone subnet that overlaps a network already connected to the Mac.
By default such a subnet is refused, so that a malicious phone cannot shadow a local network.
.TP
.BI \-U " user"
User that runs
.BR adb .
Defaults to
.IR SUDO_USER ;
required when started by launchd.
.TP
.BI \-S " serial"
Serial number of the phone to switch with
.BR adb ,
when several devices are connected
.RB ( "adb devices"
lists them). Without it, the phone is chosen only if exactly one device is ready; otherwise the problem is written to the log.
.TP
.BI \-W " user"
Unprivileged user of the worker process. Defaults to
.IR nobody .
.TP
.BI \-d " vid:pid"
Only use the device with this USB identifier (hexadecimal), for example
.IR 04e8:6864 .
.TP
.B \-v
Verbose logs.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-diagnose
Print a report for bug reports and exit. It needs no privileges and changes nothing. It shows the version, the state of the service (supervisor and worker), the USB devices that have a network, ADB or MTP interface, the ADB state, the tether's IPv4 and IPv6 routes, the DNS resolvers, the end of the log, and a plain-language diagnosis. MAC addresses are cut after the vendor part, public IPv4 and global IPv6 addresses are masked, and ADB serial numbers are not shown. Read the report before you publish it.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /var/log/rndis-tether.log
Log of the service. Lines are tagged [root] or [worker]. The worker does not write to this file: the supervisor copies its output after removing control characters, cutting long lines and limiting the rate (100 lines per 10 seconds). The supervisor reopens the file after a rotation.
.TP
.I /etc/newsyslog.d/rndis-tether.conf
Rotation of the log by
.BR newsyslog (8):
above 1 MB, five compressed archives.
.TP
.I /Users/Shared/rndis-tether.disabled
If this file exists, the service stays idle. The menu bar app creates and removes it.
.TP
.I /Users/Shared/rndis-tether.status
Current state, written by the supervisor every few seconds.
.TP
.I /Library/LaunchDaemons/io.github.rndis-tether.plist
launchd job of the service.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Normal end.
.TP
.B 1
No RNDIS device found (without \fB\-w\fR), session failure, or startup failure.
.TP
.B 2
Usage error.
.TP
.B 70
The worker could not drop its privileges.
.SH SECURITY
Only the supervisor has root privileges. It accepts six kinds of requests from the worker and validates
the values of each of them before running
.BR ifconfig (8),
.BR route (8),
.BR scutil (8)
or
.BR adb (1).
The worker cannot write core files and is limited to 128 file descriptors. It reports to the supervisor every 10 seconds,
and the supervisor replaces a worker that has been silent for 60 seconds.
See
.I SECURITY.md
and
.I docs/how-it-works.md
in the source distribution.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR adb (1),
.BR ifconfig (8),
.BR route (8),
.BR scutil (8)
.PP
